    "https://studentjob.jh.edu/sessmile.cfm": {
      "title": "Smile",
      "description": "Smile - Student Employment Opportunities - University Experiential Learning (current) Student Information Job Search Employer Information Post Job Events Student Employment Week Award Ceremony smile FAQs (current) Student Information Find Job Employer Information Post Job Events Student Employment Week Award Ceremony smile FAQs STUDENTS Search Paid Campus Internships & Jobs EMPLOYERS Post/Edit/Manage Positions GET PAID TimesheetX Resources FAQs & Instructions For Employers & Students Welcome to Hopkins SMILE SMILE is the University Experiential Learning platform that connects current students to paid campus internships and \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\temployment opportunities across Johns Hopkins University. This platform includes paid campus internships and a variety of student jobs, \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\twork-study & non work-study. Student employment and paid campus internships are some of the most valuable \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\texperiences of college life. These experiential learning opportunities provide our students the chance to: Gain power skills (success skills) Develop professional networks Sharpen business communication skills Access mentors Experience various work environments Make audacious moves Design their life path NOTE: All positions posted on SMILE are non-credit bearing, compensated via JHU payroll, and are part time. All undergraduate research positions should be posted on ForagerOne through the Hopkins Office of Undergraduate Research (HOUR) Let's Get Started! Find Position Paid campus internships, student jobs, work-study & non work-study alike [ for students ] Complete I-9 All newly hired rehired employees working in the US complete a Form I-9 [ for students ] How To Get Paid Time Tracking TimesheetX is for Hourly Student Employees [ students/Employers ] Post Position Post your paid campus internships and student jobs [ for employers ] FAQs & Instructions How do I get paid How to apply How to post a position [ students/employers ] STUDENT INFORMATION JOB SEARCH WORK STUDY EMPLOYER INFORMATION JOB POSTINGS STUDENT EMPLOYMENT WEEK KEY LINKS CONTACT US Copyright © Johns Hopkins University | University Experiential Learning. All rights reserved."
    },
